{
  "description": "Initial departments, positions, and permission assignments for the Agora incumbent migration. Mirrors a typical public administration org chart so an existing PA can map its staff 1-to-1. Seeded as real Department organizations (policy, fund, permissions, Position seats, staff invite codes) by init.py — see issue #241. Policies start founder-friendly because a fresh realm has few members; each department declares a target_policy (5-of-10) that admins ratchet up in Departments once the seats are staffed. Position salary_amount is per salary_period in the realm's accounting currency; headcount x salary is the org's personnel budget line. Each department may declare 'extensions' (domain extensions its staff can access, seeded as Extension→department grants) and 'hidden_extensions' (sidebar hide rules via MenuDepartmentVisibility, visible=False); both are templates that admins can override later in Department Management.",
  "invite": {
    "expires_in_hours": 720,
    "max_uses": 100
  },
  "departments": [
    {
      "name": "Congress",
      "description": "Supreme legislative authority. Receives root from the creator at the Beta transition and holds all realm permissions from then on; decides the move to Live by vote.",
